## Layout

- `Cargo.toml` defines the virtual workspace.
- `clippy.toml` sets the project-owned cognitive-complexity threshold.
- `crates/<<[ package_name ]>>` contains the project-owned [% if artifact_kind == "library" %]library[% else %]binary[% endif %] crate.

Prerequisites: Rust <<[ rust_version ]>> or newer.

## Setup and checks

```sh
scripts/jig setup
scripts/jig check fmt
scripts/jig check clippy
scripts/jig check test
scripts/jig check test-locked
scripts/jig check contract
```

Setup creates `Cargo.lock`; commit it so locked checks and CI use the same dependency resolution.

The workspace enables Clippy's `cognitive_complexity` nursery lint with a threshold of 20 and its `mod_module_files` restriction lint to reject `mod.rs` module layouts. Clippy describes the complexity score as a heuristic rather than an objective measurement. The strict `scripts/jig check clippy` command checks all targets and features, treats all warnings as failures, and explicitly denies `mod_module_files`, so the layout policy still applies to feature-gated modules and if a workspace member forgets to inherit workspace lints. Clippy checks compiled workspace targets rather than every tracked Rust file or code selected only on another target platform; adjust or remove this project-owned policy when it does not fit the codebase.
